\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {15.3}{\ignorespaces Distributed limiter architecture. Edge replicas consult one shared cell per key, chosen by consistent hashing so cell loss remaps only $1/C$ of keyspace; the Lua script makes check-and-admit atomic inside a cell. The dashed policy annotation is mandatory, not decorative: every replica must know what it does when the cell is unreachable (Section~\ref {subsec:ch14-failopen}).}}{914}{figure.15.3}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:ch14-distributed}{{15.3}{914}{Distributed limiter architecture. Edge replicas consult one shared cell per key, chosen by consistent hashing so cell loss remaps only $1/C$ of keyspace; the Lua script makes check-and-admit atomic inside a cell. The dashed policy annotation is mandatory, not decorative: every replica must know what it does when the cell is unreachable (Section~\ref {subsec:ch14-failopen})}{figure.15.3}{}}
